title: 'pallet-revive: bound storage deposit refunds by the held deposit'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A refund for removed contract storage is now bounded by the storage deposit the contract
    holds above its base deposit. The refund is still computed pro rata from the item and byte
    deposits recorded in the contract's `ContractInfo`, but at the end of the call stack at most
    the contract's `StorageDepositReserve` hold minus its `storage_base_deposit` is released. The
    base deposit stays on hold until the contract is terminated. The bound uses
    `Deposit::total_on_hold`, which for `PGasDeposit` is the sum of the native and PGAS holds.

    `Origin::Root` pays no storage deposit, so a contract it instantiates now records a base
    deposit of zero, and all of the slot deposits signed callers pay for it can be refunded.
    Contracts instantiated by `Origin::Root` before this change keep the base deposit recorded in
    their `ContractInfo`, although it was never held. For them, up to that amount of the slot
    deposits paid by signed callers stays on hold until the contract is terminated. There is no
    migration: `ContractInfo` does not record who instantiated a contract, so these contracts
    cannot be identified.

    The storage deposit reported by `bare_call`, `bare_instantiate`, dry runs and Ethereum
    receipts is now the amount released from the contracts' holds. After the refunds are paid,
    the deposit limit, or the Ethereum gas limit, is checked again before any charge is paid, and
    the call fails with `StorageDepositNotEnoughFunds` if it is exceeded. The deposit consumed
    rises there when a refund is not released in full.

    `PGasDeposit::refund_all` now returns the amount released from the contract's holds,
    including the burned part of the PGAS hold, as documented on `Deposit::refund_all`.
    Previously it returned the native part and only the PGAS share credited to the destination.
    The amounts credited and burned are unchanged.

    With the native deposit backend (`()`), refunds within the deposit held above the base
    deposit are unchanged. With `PGasDeposit`, an origin that is not entitled to the native part
    of a refund can see a smaller reported refund, and its deposit limit is enforced against the
    amount released from the hold. Previously the full requested refund was reported and counted
    against the limit although only part of it was released.

    No migration, configuration or runtime integration change is needed.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The refund for removed contract storage is bounded by the deposit the contract holds above
    its base deposit, and the storage deposit reported for a call is the amount that was released
    from the contracts' holds. Refunds within the deposit held above the base deposit are
    unchanged. On runtimes using `PGasDeposit`, an origin that is not entitled to the native part
    of a refund can see a smaller reported refund, and its storage deposit limit is enforced
    against the amount released from the hold. A call whose limit is exceeded this way fails with
    `StorageDepositNotEnoughFunds`. On runtimes using `PGasDeposit`, the deposit limit is checked
    against the charges minus the deposit released from the holds, while the origin is credited
    only `RefundPercent` of a released PGAS hold. The limit therefore does not cap the origin's
    out-of-pocket PGAS cost when its call releases PGAS deposits by clearing storage.
    Contracts instantiated by `Origin::Root` record a base deposit of zero, so storage deposits
    paid for them are refunded in full.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
